  "foot": "♻️ CPRP 1 · Machining & Recycling — B1+ · self-marking ♻️",
  "story": [
    "Hugo <span class=\"hl\">is</span> a machinist in a metalworking workshop. He <span class=\"hl\">operates</span> a CNC lathe and a milling machine. Every day, the cutting tools <span class=\"hl\">produce</span> a lot of swarf, and the machines <span class=\"hl\">use</span> coolant to stay cool. Safety comes first: operators <span class=\"hl\">must wear</span> glasses, and they <span class=\"hl\">mustn't pour</span> used coolant into the drain.",
    "Last month, the workshop <span class=\"hl\">started</span> a big recycling drive. First, the team <span class=\"hl\">sorted</span> the waste into three skips: one for scrap metal, one for plastic and one for cardboard. Then Hugo <span class=\"hl\">emptied</span> the coolant tank and <span class=\"hl\">sent</span> the old fluid to a treatment plant. The drive <span class=\"hl\">was harder</span> than expected, but the results <span class=\"hl\">were better</span> than last year.",
    "Since the drive began, the team <span class=\"hl\">has collected</span> two tonnes of scrap metal and <span class=\"hl\">has recycled</span> almost 90% of its waste. They <span class=\"hl\">haven't sent</span> any swarf to landfill yet. Hugo says recycling <span class=\"hl\">is cheaper</span> than throwing metal away, and it is one of <span class=\"hl\">the best</span> things the workshop has ever done. 🌱"
  ],
